   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<font face=\"Arial\">Hi, t</font><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">hank yo</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">u so much for this resource. </span><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I would like to know how to identify SNPs associated with </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">unique variance</span><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"font-family:Arial\"> beyond the common factor. If I have three variables for simplicity&#39;s sake, is this correct?</font><div><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">model &lt;- &quot;F1 =~ VAR1 + VAR2 + VAR3</font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">VAR1 ~~ SNP</font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">VAR2 ~~ SNP</font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">VAR3 ~~ SNP</font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">&quot;</font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">and then teh same terms in userGWAS (i.e., sub = c(&quot;VAR1 ~~ SNP&quot;, &quot;VAR2 ~~ SNP&quot;, &quot;VAR3 ~~ SNP&quot;))?</font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">Thanks!</font></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"Arial\">Mary</font></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "h8PghxYNAQAJ",
   "from": "Elliot Tucker-Drob",
   "author": "ac421cf36d1a4c37",
   "date": "2025-02-09T01:21:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: SNP effects on the residual (unique) variance",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">Such a model is not identified but the Qsnp statistic will be very useful here and you can perform post hoc analyses to identify the pathways that likely drive Qsnp for a particular variant as we explain here (see supplement in particular):</div><div dir=\"auto\"><div><span style=\"font-family:helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:100;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">de la Fuente, J., Davies, J., Grotzinger, A. D., Tucker-Drob, E. M., &amp; Deary. (2020). A general dimension of genetic sharing across diverse cognitive traits inferred from molecular data. </span><em style=\"font-family:helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:100;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;color:rgb(102,102,102)\">Nature Human Behaviour.</em><span style=\"font-family:helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:100;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important;color:rgb(102,102,102)\"> [de la Fuente &amp; Davies contributed equally to this work; Tucker-Drob &amp; Deary jointly directed this work] </span><a href=\"https://rdcu.be/b6SOl\" style=\"text-decoration:none;font-family:helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:100;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;color:rgb(32,144,172)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdcu.be/b6SOl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237075929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1l9uqLa4EkQrYROZcZP25O\">Link</a><span style=\"font-family:helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:100;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important;color:rgb(102,102,102)\"> </span><a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-020-00936-2#Sec21\" style=\"text-decoration:none;font-family:helvetica,arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:100;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;color:rgb(32,144,172)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-020-00936-2%23Sec21&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237075929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2h-u9LaehsKVmMh5vzCjls\">Supplements</a></div><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
